# Penny Lane, verse mm. 3-8, the chromatic progression as embellished (figure 104.3)
# Transposed to C as in fig. 104.2, four voices, one column to a bar. The soprano's held C over G
# is the 4-3 suspension resolving to B in the last bar (Pollack's "4 ---> 3").
# The lower three voices are blank in the last column; they are shown holding.
key C

system
voice "Soprano"   | C5 | Bb4 | C5 | - | -{4} | B4{3} |
voice "Alto"      | G4 | - | - | Ab4 | G4 | - |
voice "Tenor"     | E4 | Eb4 | - | - | D4 | - |
bass "Bass"       | C3{I} | - | A2 | Ab2{flat-VI} | G2{V} | - |
